DESCRIPTION:
    Unified command-line entry point for the P_300 project. Wraps the
    eight operator-facing flows behind a single command:

        python cli.py add-pattern --xlsx PATH
            Ingest one VP Pattern XLSX via add_pattern_pipeline.
            Exit 0 on successful promotion, 1 on any failure.

        python cli.py archive-pattern --xlsx PATH
            Post-ingest archive step for Pipeline A. Appends the XLSX
            to this month's zip in data/processed/ and deletes the
            original from data/historical_patterns/. Run AFTER
            add-pattern. Exit 0 on success, 1 on any failure.

        python cli.py catalog-summary [--recent N]
            Print catalog health summary via utilities/catalog_summary.
            Exit 0 if no ghost records, 1 otherwise.

        python cli.py integrity-check --xlsx PATH
            Validate a VP export against ingest_manifest.json via
            utilities/vp_export_integrity_check. Run after any VP
            version update before resuming ingest. Exit 0 = safe to
            ingest, 1 = manifest needs an edit.

        python cli.py inspect-pattern --id N [--catalog PATH]
            Print one pattern's header, raw bars, normalized bars, and
            forward labels via utilities/inspect_pattern. Stage 5
            hand-compare regression helper. Read-only. Exit 0 on
            success, 1 if --id not found.

        python cli.py daily-evaluate --xlsx PATH [--window-length 20]
                                     [--top-k 20] [--no-write-file]
                                     [--reports-dir PATH] [--no-narrator]
                                     [--clean]
            Run Pipeline B on one live `History Grid (SYMBOL).xlsx`:
            parse + normalize + match against catalog + classify +
            emit BUY/WATCH/PASS report to stdout. Optional file output
            to config.REPORTS_DIR. Read-only against the catalog
            (Stage 6 decision E -- EVAL_SET is transient in-memory).
            Optional Stage 8 narrator pass via LM Studio (default on
            per config.NARRATOR_ENABLED; --no-narrator forces off).
            --clean suppresses INFO logging and dense report; emits
            minimal banner + signal line only (batch-mode output).
            Exit 0 on success, 1 on any failure.

        python cli.py archive-eval --xlsx PATH
            Post-eval archive step for Pipeline B. Verifies a report
            exists for the symbol in REPORTS_DIR, appends the XLSX to
            this month's zip in data/processed/, and deletes the
            original from data/live/. Run AFTER daily-evaluate.
            Exit 0 on success, 1 on any failure.

        python cli.py bulk-extract [--input-dir PATH] [--master-db PATH]
                                    [--temp-db PATH] [--checkpoint PATH]
            Run Pipeline A-Bulk (WO-P300-E2.001) over every unprocessed
            file in data/bulk/ matching <years>[I]_Pattern_<SYMBOL>.xlsx.
            Writes to models/research/bulk_research.db ONLY -- never
            touches the live *catalog.db or Pipeline A/B. Checkpoint-
            resumable: a crash or interrupt picks up at the next
            unprocessed file, not from zero. All four paths are
            independently overridable (see M-075 -- master-db/temp-db
            overrides alone are NOT sufficient test isolation; always
            override checkpoint too when pointing at scratch paths).
            Exit 0 always (per-file failures are logged and left for
            retry, not treated as a CLI-level failure -- a partial run
            over many files is normal operation, not an error state).

        python cli.py phase5-analysis [--master-db PATH] [--no-backfill]
            Run WO-P300-E2.002 Phase 5: retroactive sector backfill
            (skippable via --no-backfill) + sector-stratified stats
            computation + sector_stats snapshot write + markdown report.
            Read-heavy against the research catalog; the only write is
            the backfill's sector column UPDATE (Lock+Temp-DB+Atomic
            Move) and the sector_stats DELETE+INSERT snapshot (same
            protocol). Never touches the live *catalog.db or Pipeline
            A/B. Exit 0 on success, 1 on any failure (unlike
            bulk-extract, a Phase 5 failure -- e.g. missing sector_map
            coverage -- IS a CLI-level failure; there's no per-file
            partial-progress concept here).

        python cli.py merge-research-catalog [--staging-db PATH]
                                              [--live-db PATH]
            Run WO-P300-E2.003's staging merge: copies the live catalog,
            merges every STRICT-tier bulk-scan pattern from
            models/research/bulk_research.db into the copy, runs the
            Stage 6 walk-forward eval against BOTH the untouched live
            catalog and the staging copy, writes both reports. NEVER
            touches the real live catalog.db -- promotion is a separate
            command. Exit 0 on success, 1 on failure.

        python cli.py merge-research-catalog --promote STAGING_DB_PATH
                                              [--live-db PATH]
            Separate, explicit promotion of a staging copy (built by the
            command above) to the real live catalog.db via the same
            Lock+Temp-DB+Atomic Move protocol every other catalog write
            uses. Only run this after reviewing the walk-forward reports
            from the build step. Exit 0 on success, 1 on failure.

        python cli.py ingest-mined [--csv PATH] [--input-dir PATH]
                                    [--staging-db PATH] [--live-db PATH]
            WO-P300-E3.002 Phase 2: reads an operator-approved
            mine_candidates.csv (defaults to config.MINE_REPORTS_DIR /
            config.MINE_CANDIDATES_CSV), re-reads each approved symbol's
            source grid file fresh from --input-dir (defaults to
            config.DATA_BULK_MINE -- never trusts Phase 1's in-memory
            result), audits every row via domain/mine_audit.py, and
            inserts audit-passed rows into a staging copy of the live
            catalog via infrastructure/catalog_merge_io.py. Runs the
            same M-079 staging walk-forward eval comparison merge-
            research-catalog uses. NEVER touches the real live
            catalog.db -- promotion is a separate command. Exit 0 on
            success, 1 on failure.

        python cli.py ingest-mined --promote STAGING_DB_PATH
                                    [--live-db PATH]
            Separate, explicit promotion of a staging copy (built by the
            command above) to the real live catalog.db. Reuses
            application.catalog_merge_pipeline.promote_staging_to_live
            unchanged -- same Lock+Temp-DB+Atomic Move promotion
            mechanics regardless of which pipeline built the staging
            copy. Only run this after reviewing the walk-forward
            reports from the build step. Exit 0 on success, 1 on
            failure.

        python cli.py archive-mined --xlsx PATH
            Post-ingest archive step for the "BulkAddPattern" process.
            Appends the XLSX to this month's zip in config.MINE_ARCHIVE_DIR
            (E:\\ external drive, date-first naming, no per-entry rename)
            and deletes the original from data/bulk/mine/. Run AFTER
            ingest-mined completes successfully. Exit 0 on success, 1 on
            any failure.

    Each subcommand is a thin shim -- the real work lives in the wrapped
    module. cli.py exists to remove the multi-line `python -c` invocation
    friction so daily operations are one-liners.

